      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's a bit of a gut punch to hear it framed that way, but I see the logic. When you say Candidate A is \"preferable\" for brand cohesion, are you essentially saying that Candidate B's very identity and presence would act as a dissonance for our clients? \n\nI want to be specific here for the partners. Are we talking about a risk that Candidate B's communication style or even their fundamental \"vibe\" would be perceived as less sophisticated or less \"high-end\" than what our clients are accustomed to? Basically, is the \"brand risk\" here that Candidate B just won't be able to pass as one of \"them\" in those closed-door environments?",
